-## Private Cache
+## Private Cache (2Q)
 
 Cached JPEG data may occupy at most 12 GiB. Before admitting a completed sheet, evict enough existing sheets to remain within that bound. Temporary render output is kept separately and removed on completion or failure. Eviction never deletes source footage or changes job-ticket semantics.
 
-The eviction policy is still open. Candidates are LRU, frequency-based eviction with aging, and 2Q. LRU has little bookkeeping and follows recent work quickly but is vulnerable to sequential scans. Aged frequency counts protect repeatedly popular clips but add counter maintenance and can lag a project switch. 2Q separates first-use entries from reused entries, resisting scans at the cost of extra queues and a queue-size parameter. None changes the external interface, queue concurrency, or disk budget.
+The cache uses a 2Q replacement policy to separate first-use sheets from reused sheets:
+
+- **First-in probation queue (`A1in`)**: A FIFO queue holding newly rendered sheets on their first admission. Bounded by a configurable byte share (`Kin`) of the 12 GiB budget.
+- **Main protected queue (`Am`)**: An LRU queue holding sheets that have demonstrated reuse. Bounded by the remaining byte budget (`12 GiB - Kin`).
+- **Ghost queue (`A1out`)**: A FIFO queue holding only cache keys (no JPEG bytes) for sheets recently evicted from `A1in`, bounded by entry count (`Kout`).
+
+On a cache hit in `Am`, the entry moves to the most-recently-used position of `Am`. On a cache miss whose key is present in `A1out`, the newly rendered sheet is admitted directly to `Am` (and its ghost entry is removed from `A1out`), protecting revisited sheets from scan eviction. On a cache miss whose key is not in `A1out`, the newly rendered sheet is admitted to `A1in`.
+
+When admitting a sheet would exceed 12 GiB, the worker evicts entries before admission until `usedBytes + newSheetBytes <= 12 GiB`. If `A1in` exceeds `Kin` (or `Am` is empty), the oldest entry in `A1in` is evicted and its key is recorded in `A1out`; otherwise the least-recently-used entry in `Am` is evicted.
+
+## Decisions & Alternatives
+
+| Decision | Chosen | Alternatives Considered | Rationale |
+|----------|--------|------------------------|-----------|
+| Cache eviction policy | 2Q (`A1in` / `Am` / `A1out`) | LRU, Frequency-based eviction with aging | Protects repeatedly accessed comparison sheets from one-off sequential screening scans while adapting faster than aged frequency counters when editors switch projects. Extra queue bookkeeping and size-split tuning remain private to the preview worker. |
+
